<h2 data-start=3D"3642" data-end=3D"3671" class=3D"">3. Relations entre mod=
=C3=A8les</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3673" data-end=3D"3843" class=3D"">Les relations entre mod=
=C3=A8les permettent de d=C3=A9finir des associations logiques entre les di=
ff=C3=A9rentes entit=C3=A9s de l=E2=80=99application. Django supporte plusi=
eurs types de relations :</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3845" data-end=3D"3893" class=3D"">3.1. Relations <code d=
ata-start=3D"3864" data-end=3D"3876">ForeignKey</code> (Un =C3=A0 plusieurs=
)</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3895" data-end=3D"4052" class=3D"">Une relation <code data=
-start=3D"3908" data-end=3D"3920">ForeignKey</code> est utilis=C3=A9e pour =
d=C3=A9finir une relation <strong data-start=3D"3960" data-end=3D"3978">un =
=C3=A0 plusieurs</strong> entre deux mod=C3=A8les. Par exemple, un <code da=
ta-start=3D"4015" data-end=3D"4021">Post</code> peut appartenir =C3=A0 un <=
code data-start=3D"4043" data-end=3D"4051">Auteur</code>.</p>
