<h3 data-start=3D"6822" data-end=3D"6863" class=3D"">3.1 Introduction au fi=
ltrage complexe</h3>
<p data-start=3D"6865" data-end=3D"7070" class=3D"">Le filtrage complexe da=
ns DRF implique g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement des filtres sur des relations entre =
mod=C3=A8les (comme <code data-start=3D"6968" data-end=3D"6980">ForeignKey<=
/code>, <code data-start=3D"6982" data-end=3D"6994">ManyToMany</code>) ou d=
es filtres conditionnels qui combinent plusieurs crit=C3=A8res de filtrage.=
</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"7072" data-end=3D"7086" class=3D"">Exemple :</h4>
<p data-start=3D"7088" data-end=3D"7259" class=3D"">Imaginons que nous ayon=
s un mod=C3=A8le <code data-start=3D"7123" data-end=3D"7132">Comment</code>=
